==============================================================================
VERDICT: PROVEN, in two tiers
  OFF, TIER 1 -- general to LangGraph + PostgresSaver, nothing to do with
       deepagents: two workers on one thread_id fork the checkpoint chain;
       the loser's put_writes is silently discarded while it reports
       success; its committed work, terminal checkpoint included, is
       unreachable from the tip; the answer it returned to its caller
       contradicts the thread. Both workers exit 0. Nothing warns.
  OFF, TIER 2 -- specific to deepagents' DeltaChannel transcript: the
       surviving branch's message list is MALFORMED -- a tool_result whose
       tool_use was silently discarded and is stored NOWHERE, alongside a
       tool_use whose result is on the abandoned branch. A plain
       MessagesState graph forks identically but leaves each branch
       internally consistent, because its full list lives in its own blob.
  ON:  the same zombie's writes were refused by Postgres, the chain did not
       fork, and the survivor's thread is intact and usable -- on both the
       pipeline path and the supports_pipeline=False fallback.
==============================================================================
